cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use utu in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: utu
abstract: >-
  utu is a Python library of solar physics utilities built on named-arrays,
  named for the Sumerian god of the sun. Its spectrum module computes the
  emission lines of an optically thin plasma from the CHIANTI atomic database
  through fiasco: which ions are abundant enough to contribute over a range
  of wavelengths, the intensity of every line for a given temperature,
  density, and emission measure, and the contribution function of each line,
  along with the spectroscopic name of each ion and stem plots which label
  the brightest lines. Its rotation module differentially rotates
  helioprojective coordinates to a new time, carrying each point along the
  solar surface, which turns faster at the equator than at the poles, and
  viewing it from where the observer has moved to. Inputs and results are
  named arrays, so they carry physical units and broadcast against each
  other by axis name.
authors:
  - family-names: Smart
    given-names: Roy T.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9997-5515"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sun-data/utu"
url: "https://utu.readthedocs.io"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - solar physics
  - spectroscopy
  - CHIANTI
  - differential rotation
  - named arrays
